{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "For U1, integrate the Hortonworks Connector for Teradata as the supported way to connect Sqoop to Teradata, since the direct JDBC driver causes NPE.",
    "For U2, introduce a new configuration property 'xd.log.dir' with default value '${xd.home}/logs' to maintain backward compatibility while allowing external configuration (e.g., '/var/logs/spring-xd' for RPM).",
    "For U3 and U5, move message-bus and serialization codec into a new or existing 'spring-bus' repository, adjusting Maven coordinates and package structure to avoid conflicts.",
    "For U4, move input/output type conversion logic to 'spring-cloud-dataflow' project, ensuring the new module can be consumed by Spring XD and custom modules.",
    "For U6, implement a singlenode Module Launcher that runs all XD Admin SPI operations in a single JVM, leveraging existing Module Launcher abstractions.",
    "For U7, implement a Diego Receptor-based ModuleLauncher and XD Admin SPI using Spring Cloud Cloud Foundry libraries, targeting CF Lattice/Diego.",
    "For U8, conduct a feasibility investigation only; no production implementation is required in this increment. Prototype using Spring Cloud service discovery (Eureka/Consul) for module self-registration."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Developer has access to a Teradata database instance for testing U1.",
    "Developer has access to a CF Lattice/Diego environment for testing U7.",
    "The 'spring-bus' and 'spring-cloud-dataflow' repositories exist and are ready to accept the moved code.",
    "Spring XD codebase is modular enough to extract message-bus, type conversion, and serialization codec without major refactoring of dependent modules.",
    "Documentation updates are limited to configuration references and migration notes.",
    "Effort estimates assume a single developer with expertise in Spring, Sqoop, Hadoop, and Cloud Foundry.",
    "No additional infrastructure setup (e.g., CI/CD pipelines for new modules) is required beyond what's described.",
    "Testing for each user story is included in the respective activities; no separate integration test phase is estimated."
  ],
